<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador int'l reserves slip to $1.84 bln Jan 17.</title>
<headline>Ecuador int'l reserves slip to $1.84 bln Jan 17.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Friday its net international reserves stood at $1.841 billion on January 17, down $3 million from the week before.</p>
<p>In December 1996, international reserves grew $180 million.</p>
<p>The Central Bank gave no reason for the fall of reserves.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.832 billion at the end of last year, up $276 million from the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
